---
description: TypeScript / React app conventions and the frontend API seam
globs: ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Strict TypeScript, tabs, `camelCase`, React function components with hooks.
  Import from `src` via the `@/` alias. Lines under 100 chars. No JS linter is
  configured — match the surrounding file exactly.
- Export types used in exported signatures; keep imports sorted within groups
  (third-party, local, relative). No magic numbers; 3+ params take a typed options
  object. Reuse or extend existing types and utilities before adding new ones.
- Prefer `@wordpress/components` for UI. Single `h1` per admin screen; sections
  start at `h2`.
- Declarative React: derive with `useMemo` over `useEffect` chains, update state
  in handlers, controlled forms, compute at render. Hooks return state and actions,
  not elements. Type no-arg callbacks as `VoidFunction`.
- Conditional render `cond && <el>` (reserve `? … : null` for numeric/string).
  Avoid nested ternaries, trivial memoization, unnecessary ARIA, and props that
  repeat defaults. JSX over `createElement`. No barrel `index.ts` re-export files.
- User-facing strings translated with the `translate` text domain and
  `CONTEXT.md` vocabulary; `// translators:` on the line directly above the string.
- `src/shared/lib/languages/flagSpritePositions.ts` is generated from `styles.css`
  by `yarn generate:flag-positions` — never hand-edit it.

App boundaries:
- Three apps under `src/apps/{admin,setup,translatewp}`; an app never imports from
  another app. Shared code lives in `src/shared`.
- All server access goes through `src/shared/api/{admin,setup,wordpress}.ts` and
  the TanStack Query option builders — no ad-hoc `fetch` in components.

Verify with `yarn test` (Jest) and `yarn build`.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md`.
